<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Abomey</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Abomey is a town in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benin-empire">Benin</a>, the capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-dahomey">Kingdom of Dahomey</a> from the seventeenth century until 1894. Each king built his own palace there, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/royal-palaces-of-abomey">Royal Palaces of Abomey</a>, with their painted clay bas-reliefs recording the kingdom's history, were made a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco-world-heritage-site">UNESCO World Heritage Site</a> in 1985. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/behanzin">Behanzin</a> burned much of the town before the French entered it in November 1892.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/abomey.jpg" alt="Abomey" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ji-Elle · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rue_d%27Abomey_(1).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
